WEBVTT

00:01:58.840 --> 00:02:01.116
People who experienced a lot of stress

00:02:01.140 --> 00:02:03.080
but did not view stress as harmful

00:02:03.104 --> 00:02:04.781
were no more likely to die.

00:02:04.805 --> 00:02:08.348
In fact, they had the lowest risk of dying

00:02:08.372 --> 00:02:09.672
of anyone in the study,

00:02:09.696 --> 00:02:12.153
including people
who had relatively little stress.

00:02:12.896 --> 00:02:15.516
Now the researchers estimated
that over the eight years

00:02:15.540 --> 00:02:17.110
they were tracking deaths,

00:02:17.134 --> 00:02:20.310
182,000 Americans died prematurely,

00:02:20.334 --> 00:02:21.772
not from stress,

00:02:21.796 --> 00:02:24.977
but from the belief
that stress is bad for you.

00:02:25.001 --> 00:02:26.233
(Laughter)

00:02:26.257 --> 00:02:29.299
That is over 20,000 deaths a year.

00:02:29.931 --> 00:02:32.735
Now, if that estimate is correct,